			<Properties>
				<ProtectedString name="Source"><![CDATA[--[==[
══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
BT SETTINGS — HOW TO ADD FEATURES  (a guide, not code)
Script · ReplicatedStorage > BTSettings · name: HowToAddFeatures
In Studio set Enabled = false (old name: Disabled = true). Everything in this
file is a comment, so it can never run anyway.
══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

THE 5 FILES
	ReplicatedStorage    > BTSettings > Config            ← you edit this to add things
	ReplicatedStorage    > BTSettings > HowToAddFeatures  ← this guide
	ServerScriptService  > BTSettings > Server
	StarterPlayerScripts > BTSettings > UI                ← draws the panel, sends signals
	StarterPlayerScripts > BTSettings > Features          ← built-in features
	(ReplicatedStorage > BTSettings > BTSettingsRemotes is made by the Server
	 when the game runs — never create it yourself.)
	ReplicatedStorage    > BTSettings > EnvironmentCycle  ← live environment timer
	                                    (edit its Settings, read its HowToUse)

YOUR OWN FEATURES = Config lines + ONE small receiver script of your own.
You never have to open UI or Features. Put your receiver scripts inside the
BTSettings folders (StarterPlayerScripts > BTSettings or
ServerScriptService > BTSettings), so nothing is loose.


──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
STEP 0 — WORDS YOU WILL SEE
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
tab      One category page (Graphics, Skybox, Servers, Player, Audio).
         It shows as a big card on the home screen of the panel.
control  One thing inside a tab: a button, a toggle (on/off switch),
         a slider, a choice (pick one), or a section heading.
action   What happens when the player uses a control. The panel only
         SENDS A SIGNAL. A small receiver script RECEIVES the signal and
         does the real work.
id       A unique short name like "fun_glow". Use letters, numbers and _.
         Two controls must NEVER share the same id.


──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
STEP 1 — ADD A NEW TAB  (Config → Config.tabs, paste before the last "}")
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
	{
		id = "fun",                -- unique, lowercase, no spaces
		title = "Fun",             -- big name on the home card
		icon = "★",                -- one symbol or emoji
		desc = "Silly extras",     -- short line under the title
		isNew = true,              -- optional: shows a small NEW badge
		controls = {
			-- put controls here (STEP 2)
		},
	},


──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
STEP 2 — CONTROL TEMPLATES  (paste inside a tab's  controls = { ... })
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
2a) SECTION — a small grey heading. Every control below it (until the next
    section) is grouped under it.
	{ type = "section", title = "Extras" },

2b) BUTTON — sends NO value. Good for "do it now" things.
	{
		type = "button",
		id = "fun_confetti",
		title = "Confetti",                  -- name on the card
		desc = "Throws confetti on screen.", -- small grey text (optional)
		buttonText = "Throw!",               -- text on the button
		style = "primary",                   -- "primary" (accent color) or "secondary" (dark)
		notify = "Confetti thrown!",         -- optional pop-up after pressing
		action = { kind = "bindable", name = "FunConfetti" },
	},

2c) TOGGLE — an on/off switch. Sends true (on) or false (off).
	{
		type = "toggle",
		id = "fun_glow",
		title = "Glow",
		desc = "Makes your sword glow.",
		default = false,                     -- start value: true or false
		action = { kind = "bindable", name = "FunGlow" },
	},

2d) SLIDER — sends a NUMBER between min and max.
	{
		type = "slider",
		id = "fun_speed",
		title = "Spin speed",
		desc = "How fast the coin spins.",
		min = 0,                             -- smallest value
		max = 100,                           -- biggest value
		step = 1,                            -- 1 = whole numbers, 0.1 = one decimal
		default = 50,                        -- start value
		format = "%d%%",                     -- how the number is shown:
		                                     --   "%d" = 50   "%.1f" = 50.0
		                                     --   "%d%%" = 50%   "%.1f h" = 14.0 h
		action = { kind = "bindable", name = "FunSpeed" },
	},

2e) CHOICE — pick ONE option. Sends the chosen option's id (text).
	style = "cards" → big side-by-side cards (like the quality preset)
	style = "cycle" → one row, every tap moves to the next option
	{
		type = "choice",
		id = "fun_color",
		title = "Sword color",
		style = "cycle",
		default = "Red",
		options = {
			{ id = "Red",  title = "Red",  desc = "Hot and fast" },
			{ id = "Blue", title = "Blue", desc = "Cool and calm", descBn = "ঠান্ডা ও শান্ত" },
		},
		notify = "%s selected",              -- %s becomes the option title
		action = { kind = "bindable", name = "FunColor" },
	},

2f) CUSTOM — a hand-made page part (programmers only):
	{ type = "custom", id = "fun_board", builder = "FunBoard" },
	Then in the UI script, section [12] Builders, add:
	ctx.builders.FunBoard = function(ctx, parent, def) ... return {} end

Every field, explained:
	type        "section" | "button" | "toggle" | "slider" | "choice" | "custom"
	id          unique name (not needed for "section")
	title       big text
	desc        small grey text (optional)
	descBn      Bangla version of desc (optional, see Config.ui.language)
	default     start value (leave it out → toggle: false, slider: min,
	            choice: first option)
	min/max/step/format   sliders only
	options/style         choice only
	buttonText/style      button only
	notify      optional pop-up text after the player changes it
	isNew       true = show a NEW badge
	action      what to send (STEP 3). On a toggle/slider/choice you may leave
	            it out to only REMEMBER the value (read it with GetValue, see
	            ADVANCED).


──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
STEP 3 — BINDABLE OR REMOTE?  (what happens when the player presses it)
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
action = { kind = "bindable", name = "FunGlow" }
	The signal stays INSIDE THE SAME PLAYER'S DEVICE. Use it for things only
	that player should see or hear: graphics, camera, sounds, UI.
	Who listens: a LocalScript (in StarterPlayerScripts > BTSettings).

action = { kind = "remote", name = "FunGiveHat" }
	The signal goes from the player's device TO THE SERVER. Use it when the
	server must do something (change the world for everyone, give items...).
	Who listens: a Script (in ServerScriptService > BTSettings).

action = { kind = "internal", name = "resetAll" }
	A built-in panel command. Only "resetAll" exists right now.

What value arrives?
	button  → nothing (no value)
	toggle  → true or false
	slider  → a number
	choice  → the option id (text), for example "Low"

You do NOT create the events yourself. They are made by name:
	bindable → created on each player's device by the UI when the game starts
	remote   → created by the Server script when the server starts
	           (a device cannot create events the server can hear)
	All of them live in  ReplicatedStorage > BTSettings > BTSettingsRemotes.

What happens step by step when a player flips a toggle:
	1. UI remembers the new value (true/false)
	2. UI fires the event named in action.name with that value
	3. your receiver script's function runs with that value
	4. (optional) UI shows the "notify" pop-up

	Click sound: every button, toggle, slider, choice and tab card you add in
	Config plays the UI click sound by itself (Config.sounds). No extra work.


──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
STEP 4 — RECEIVER SCRIPTS (copy, paste, change the event name)
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
4a) BINDABLE receiver → LocalScript in StarterPlayer > StarterPlayerScripts > BTSettings

	local ReplicatedStorage = game:GetService("ReplicatedStorage")
	local remotes = ReplicatedStorage:WaitForChild("BTSettings"):WaitForChild("BTSettingsRemotes")
	local ev = remotes:WaitForChild("BTSettingsShadows")   -- the action.name from Config

	ev.Event:Connect(function(value)
		-- value is true or false for a toggle, a number for a slider
		print("Shadows toggle is now", value)
	end)

4b) REMOTE receiver → Script in ServerScriptService > BTSettings

	local Players = game:GetService("Players")
	local ReplicatedStorage = game:GetService("ReplicatedStorage")
	local remotes = ReplicatedStorage:WaitForChild("BTSettings"):WaitForChild("BTSettingsRemotes")
	local ev = remotes:WaitForChild("ResetLighting")       -- the action.name from Config
	local lastUse = {}

	ev.OnServerEvent:Connect(function(player, value)
		-- 1) Too fast? (hackers can fire 1000 times a second)
		local now = os.clock()
		if lastUse[player] and now - lastUse[player] < 0.5 then return end
		lastUse[player] = now
		-- 2) Wrong type? (a slider must send a number)
		if typeof(value) ~= "number" then return end
		-- 3) Broken or out of range? (value ~= value catches NaN)
		if value ~= value or value < 0 or value > 100 then return end
		-- 4) Now it is safe to use
		print(player.Name, "sent", value)
	end)

	Players.PlayerRemoving:Connect(function(player) lastUse[player] = nil end)

!! SECURITY WARNING !!
	Anything sent with kind = "remote" comes from the player's device, and a
	hacker can change it to ANY value of ANY type. The server receiver must
	ALWAYS check speed, type and range (like 4b) before using it. Never let a
	remote give money, items or admin powers just because the client asked.


──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
STEP 5 — FULL WORKED EXAMPLE: a "Fun" tab with a toggle and a button
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
5.1  In Config → Config.tabs, add this block after the Audio tab:

	{
		id = "fun",
		title = "Fun",
		icon = "★",
		desc = "Glow and confetti",
		isNew = true,
		controls = {
			{ type = "section", title = "Effects" },
			{
				type = "toggle",
				id = "fun_glow",
				title = "Character glow",
				desc = "A soft light around your character (only you see it).",
				default = false,
				action = { kind = "bindable", name = "FunGlow" },
			},
			{
				type = "button",
				id = "fun_confetti",
				title = "Confetti",
				desc = "Throws confetti for everyone.",
				buttonText = "Throw!",
				style = "primary",
				notify = "Confetti thrown!",
				action = { kind = "remote", name = "FunConfetti" },
			},
		},
	},

5.2  The toggle is "bindable" → make a LocalScript named FunGlow in
     StarterPlayer > StarterPlayerScripts > BTSettings:

	local Players = game:GetService("Players")
	local ReplicatedStorage = game:GetService("ReplicatedStorage")
	local remotes = ReplicatedStorage:WaitForChild("BTSettings"):WaitForChild("BTSettingsRemotes")
	local glowEvent = remotes:WaitForChild("FunGlow")
	local player = Players.LocalPlayer
	local light = nil

	local function setGlow(on)
		if light then
			light:Destroy()
			light = nil
		end
		local root = player.Character and player.Character:FindFirstChild("HumanoidRootPart")
		if on and root then
			light = Instance.new("PointLight")
			light.Range = 12
			light.Parent = root
		end
	end

	glowEvent.Event:Connect(function(value)
		setGlow(value == true)
	end)

5.3  The button is "remote" → make a Script named FunConfetti in
     ServerScriptService > BTSettings:

	local Players = game:GetService("Players")
	local ReplicatedStorage = game:GetService("ReplicatedStorage")
	local remotes = ReplicatedStorage:WaitForChild("BTSettings"):WaitForChild("BTSettingsRemotes")
	local confettiEvent = remotes:WaitForChild("FunConfetti")
	local lastUse = {}

	confettiEvent.OnServerEvent:Connect(function(player)
		local now = os.clock()
		if lastUse[player] and now - lastUse[player] < 10 then return end -- once per 10 s
		lastUse[player] = now
		local root = player.Character and player.Character:FindFirstChild("HumanoidRootPart")
		if not root then return end
		local burst = Instance.new("ParticleEmitter")
		burst.Rate = 0
		burst.Parent = root
		burst:Emit(60)
		task.delay(3, function() burst:Destroy() end)
	end)

	Players.PlayerRemoving:Connect(function(player) lastUse[player] = nil end)

5.4  Press Play. Open the panel → the new "Fun" card has a NEW badge. The
     toggle switches the glow, the button throws confetti for everyone.
     Check Output: warnings start with [BTSettings] and name the exact line.


──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
STEP 6 — CHECK THE OUTPUT WINDOW
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
When the game starts, the UI checks Config and prints clear warnings, e.g.
	[BTSettings] Tab 'fun', control 'fun_glow': action.kind must be 'bindable', 'remote' or 'internal'
A broken control is skipped; everything else keeps working. Fix the line the
warning names and press Play again.
If a built-in feature breaks, Output says which part, e.g.
	[BTSettings] Features: Audio section failed: <error>


──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ADVANCED (programmers)
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
All lines below start from:
	local remotes = game:GetService("ReplicatedStorage"):WaitForChild("BTSettings"):WaitForChild("BTSettingsRemotes")

• Read any remembered value (from any LocalScript):
	print(remotes:WaitForChild("BTSettingsGetValue"):Invoke("audio_master"))
• Show a pop-up in the panel style:
	remotes:WaitForChild("BTSettingsNotify"):Fire({
		title = "Hello", message = "Shown in the panel style", icon = "★",
		sticky = false,            -- true = stays until closed with ✕
		critical = false,          -- true = shows even if the player turned pop-ups off
		actions = { { text = "Open Audio", tab = "audio" } },
	})
• Open the panel on a tab:
	remotes:WaitForChild("BTSettingsOpenTab"):Fire("graphics")
• Hide / show the floating button (e.g. during a cutscene):
	remotes:WaitForChild("BTSettingsSetFloatingButton"):Fire(false)  -- hide
	remotes:WaitForChild("BTSettingsSetFloatingButton"):Fire(true)   -- show
• Add a control while the game runs (fire AFTER the panel loaded):
	remotes:WaitForChild("BTSettingsAddControl"):Fire({
		tab = "player", section = "character",
		type = "toggle", id = "my_toggle", title = "My toggle", default = false,
		action = { kind = "bindable", name = "MyToggle" },
	})
• New control TYPES (dropdown, textbox, keybind ...): in the UI script,
  section [10] Controls, add Controls.register("dropdown", function(parent, def) ... end).
• Colors: Config.theme (change `active`). Floating button: Config.floatingButton.
• Renaming the system: change Config.PREFIX. The three "BTSettings" folders
  and the script names are Studio names you rename yourself (UI and Features
  find Config with one line at the top: ReplicatedStorage:WaitForChild("BTSettings")).
══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
]==]
]]></ProtectedString>
